{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-topological-defects","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:topological-defects","kind":"remark","title":"Topological signatures in large-scale structure","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-characteristic-classes","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-characteristic-classes","tags":["topology","large-scale-structure","observation"],"text":"topological-defects.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:topological-defects\"></a><p>The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SO}(3)</code> holonomy of the bulk bundle (<a href=\"#ex:c-quantum-universe\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code>-quantum universe</a>) and the monodromy fixed points of the (<a href=\"#def:quantum-characteristic-classes\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting-construction\">quantum characteristic classes</a>) may leave topological imprints on the large-scale distribution of matter. Such imprints include preferred filamentary alignments or voids correlated with the brane tower structure (<a href=\"#def:recursive-brane-tower\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">recursive brane tower</a>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/topological-defects.md","heading":"Remark","number":"17.13.5","page":"b/rem-topological-defects","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
